From f9c61d9d30a2ec799653582b27106a60a3cf942c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Hughes <ryan@heyoodle.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:31:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1078/1078] PCI: Keep hotplug bridges below a switch to their
 share of bus numbers

When a switch is hot-added below a hotplug bridge, pci_hp_add_bridge()
hands it every bus number up to the subordinate of the slot, and
pci_scan_child_bus_extend() divides them between the switch's hotplug
downstream ports. Each port is then extended to at least
pci_hotplug_bus_size - 1 numbers, capped only at the end of the parent
bus, so with "pci=hpbussize" larger than the share the first port takes
all that are left. The ports after it are given a secondary bus past
the parent's subordinate and nothing behind them is enumerated.

This shows up on software connection manager USB4 hosts that leave the
tunnel root ports unconfigured, where hpbussize is the only way to give
a root port bus numbers for a dock. With hpbussize=0x20 and a CalDigit
TS4 (Goshen Ridge), its first downstream port took buses 04-20 and the
port leading to the dock's Ethernet controller was left with:

  pci_bus 000b:21: busn_res: can not insert [bus 21-20] under [bus 02-20] (conflicts with (null) [bus 02-20])

Apply the minimum only to hotplug bridges that were not given a share,
such as root ports scanned at boot, and let the others keep to it.
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt | 3 +++
 drivers/pci/probe.c                             | 7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
index 489de55bb5..b21d66a8f2 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
@@ -5227,6 +5227,9 @@ Kernel parameters
 				Default size is 2 megabytes.
 		hpbussize=nn	The minimum amount of additional bus numbers
 				reserved for buses below a hotplug bridge.
+				A hotplug bridge below a hot-added switch
+				gets its share of the switch's bus numbers
+				instead.
 				Default is 1.
 		realloc=	Enable/disable reallocating PCI bridge resources
 				if allocations done by BIOS are too small to
diff --git a/drivers/pci/probe.c b/drivers/pci/probe.c
index dd0abbc63e..876cf0dfed 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/probe.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/probe.c
@@ -3168,10 +3168,13 @@ static unsigned int pci_scan_child_bus_extend(struct pci_bus *bus,
 	/*
 	 * Make sure a hotplug bridge has at least the minimum requested
 	 * number of buses but allow it to grow up to the maximum available
-	 * bus number if there is room.
+	 * bus number if there is room. A bridge that was handed a share of
+	 * its parent's buses keeps to that share instead: the rest is meant
+	 * for its siblings, and growing to the minimum would leave the
+	 * hotplug bridges after it on the parent bus without any.
 	 */
 	if (bus->self && bus->self->is_hotplug_bridge) {
-		used_buses = max(available_buses, pci_hotplug_bus_size - 1);
+		used_buses = available_buses ?: pci_hotplug_bus_size - 1;
 		if (max - start < used_buses) {
 			max = start + used_buses;
 
